# Generated catalog. Reproducible offline from the committed sources/ tier files.
data-pipeline/out/

# Faculty pipeline — intermediate artifacts, git-ignored per
# docs/FACULTY_PIPELINE.md §3 (regenerated by running the pipeline).
#
# `output/` is a DELIBERATE exclusion, not an oversight, and this repo is
# public. master.csv holds several hundred named academics' emails and phone
# numbers. Each field is already public on its own university's site, but
# aggregating them into one downloadable file is a materially different thing
# from them being scattered across 268 domains — that concentration is exactly
# what makes scraped directory data valuable to spammers. Anyone who needs the
# CSVs can regenerate them: `python -m faculty_pipeline all`.
#
# Do not commit these, and do not `git add -f` them, without the repo owner
# deciding to publish that aggregate. Decision recorded 2026-08-09.
faculty-pipeline/data/
faculty-pipeline/cache/
faculty-pipeline/checkpoints/
faculty-pipeline/logs/
faculty-pipeline/output/

# Coverage data (incl. macOS " 2" conflict copies)
.coverage*

# vitest transient bundles
*.timestamp-*.mjs

# Local, per-machine Claude settings
.claude/settings.local*.json

# Env / editor
.env
.DS_Store
.superpowers/
